<title>USA: Metro Global to buy back 200,000 shares.</title>
<headline>Metro Global to buy back 200,000 shares.</headline>
<dateline>CRANSTON, R.I. 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Metro Global Media Inc said Tuesday its board had authorized the repurchase of up to 200,000 shares of common stock.</p>
<p>The company said the board took the step because of the recent price decline of its stock and the current book value of its common shares, which was $2 as of the March 1.</p>
<p>The company said the repurchase is an &quot;excellent investment&quot; based on its current price.</p>
<p>The stock closed at 1-5/8 on April 25.</p>
</text>
